abstract: >-
  MES (Motor Engagement Signal) is an open-source Python library and companion
  web application that converts clinical-style EEG recordings into a single
  calibrated 0-100 score reflecting motor-cortical engagement during movement
  or motor-imagery tasks. It combines mu/beta event-related desynchronization,
  a lateralization index, movement-related cortical potentials, and an ONNX
  ensemble of Riemannian and deep-learning classifiers, with weights fit
  against dataset-provided labels to avoid circularity. MES targets stroke and
  spinal-cord-injury rehabilitation researchers who need interpretable,
  session-comparable endpoints rather than decoding accuracy alone, and runs on
  low-channel ambulatory hardware such as OpenBCI Cyton+Daisy.
